  "description": "Enterprise PDF generation and manipulation for .NET. Fluent layout engine for building complex documents with automatic pagination, interactive forms, digital signing, merge, encrypt, text extraction, and PDF/A compliance — all with zero managed runtime dependencies.",
  "id": "FolioPDF",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-14T08:35:56.753Z",
  "licenseFile": "LICENSE.md",
  "licenseUrl": "https://aka.ms/deprecateLicenseUrl",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "QaAC64pf42l4Or5MJMtusZqROweaIp7cDeeDweNh3epG6c5R+2W+BN/YYq7H6TTsK0WNkvXppdsDyv+GSKvCog==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 46280712,
  "published": "2026-11-14T08:31:03.05Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2026.11.1 (bug fixes since 2026.4.1):\n- GenerateImages renders the page at the requested RasterDpi. At any DPI other than 72, including the default of 150, the page was drawn at 72-DPI size into the top-left corner of an otherwise blank image.\n- GenerateImages rounds image sizes up instead of truncating, so the bottom and right edges of a page are no longer cut off. Where a page is not a whole number of pixels the image is 1 px larger than before (A4 at 150 DPI: 1240 × 1755 instead of 1239 × 1754); at 72 DPI sizes are unchanged.\n- GenerateImages validates its arguments when called: a null document, RasterDpi of 0 or less, Quality outside 1–100, or an undefined ImageFormat throws ArgumentException.\n- Documents longer than 250 pages are no longer silently truncated. A page set may now produce up to 10,000 pages; content that still has not finished at that point throws InvalidOperationException instead of being dropped.\n- GenerateSvg returns exactly one SVG per page for multi-page documents.\n- Font memory is bounded: each font file is held once in native memory and font collections are pooled per document instead of kept per thread, which fixes unbounded memory growth in long-running servers.\n- Folio's native libraries are loaded by their own versioned file names first, so a qpdf binary from another package (e.g. QuestPDF) in the same output folder can no longer be loaded in place of Folio's.\n- SVG images keep the aspect ratio of their viewBox instead of being laid out as 1:1.\n- RegisterFont now throws on an empty stream or data that is not a valid font, and RegisterFontWithCustomName rejects a blank name; both previously accepted the input silently.",
  "verbatimVersion": "2026.11.1",
